---
name: code-reviews
description: Deep code review + QA validation for wp-media/backwpup-pro. With a PR number, checks out the branch, reviews the code, runs the QA pipeline, and posts a single combined comment. Without arguments, fetches all open PRs in the "Ready for Review" column of the team board and reviews each one.
---

# Code Reviews

Repository: `wp-media/backwpup-pro`
Board: `https://github.com/orgs/wp-media/projects/116/views/20`

When the user runs:
- `/code-reviews 1234` → review PR #1234 and post findings as a PR comment
- `/code-reviews` → fetch all PRs in **Ready for Review** from the board, then review each one

---

## Step 0 — Prepare the environment

Save the current branch so you can return to it after the review:

```bash
ORIGINAL_BRANCH=$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD)
```

Checkout the PR branch locally:

```bash
gh pr checkout <number> --repo wp-media/backwpup-pro
```

---

## Step 1 — Resolve target PRs

### With a PR number

```bash
gh pr view <number> --repo wp-media/backwpup-pro --json number,title,body,baseRefName,headRefName,files,additions,deletions,url,closingIssuesReferences
```

### Without arguments — query the board

```bash
gh api graphql -f query='
query {
  organization(login: "wp-media") {
    projectV2(number: 116) {
      items(first: 100) {
        nodes {
          fieldValues(first: 20) {
            nodes {
              ... on ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue {
                name
                field { ... on ProjectV2SingleSelectField { name } }
              }
            }
          }
          content {
            ... on PullRequest {
              number title state url

